      "source": {
        "topic_name": "The Sixth Measure: (seeking refuge with Allah [SWT] upon starting salat)",
        "text": "Jubayr Ibn Mut'im (RA) reported: \"I saw the Prophet (∩╖║) A say, \n\n<ar> ╪º┘ä┘ä┘ç┘Å ╪ú┘Ä┘â┘Æ╪¿┘Ä┘Ç╪▒┘Å ┘â┘Ä╪¿┘Ç┘è╪▒╪º ╪î</ar>\n<ar>╪º┘ä┘ä┘ç┘Å ╪ú┘Ä┘â┘Æ╪¿┘Ä┘Ç╪▒┘Å ┘â┘Ä╪¿┘Ç┘è╪▒╪º ╪î</ar>\n<ar>╪º┘ä┘ä┘ç┘Å ╪ú┘Ä┘â┘Æ╪¿┘Ä┘Ç╪▒┘Å ┘â┘Ä╪¿┘Ç┘è╪▒╪º ╪î</ar>\n<ar>┘ê┘Ä╪º┘ä┘Æ╪¡┘Ä┘Ç┘à┘Æ╪»┘Å ┘ä┘ä┘ç┘É ┘â┘Ä╪½┘Ç┘è╪▒╪º ╪î</ar>\n<ar>┘ê┘Ä╪º┘ä┘Æ╪¡┘Ä┘Ç┘à┘Æ╪»┘Å ┘ä┘ä┘ç┘É ┘â┘Ä╪½┘Ç┘è╪▒╪º ╪î</ar>\n<ar>┘ê┘Ä╪º┘ä┘Æ╪¡┘Ä┘Ç┘à┘Æ╪»┘Å ┘ä┘ä┘ç┘É ┘â┘Ä╪½┘Ç┘è╪▒╪º ╪î</ar>\n<ar>┘ê┘Ä╪│┘Å╪¿┘Æ┘Ç╪¡╪º┘å┘Ä ╪º┘ä┘ä┘ç┘É ╪¿┘â┘Æ┘Ç╪▒┘Ä╪⌐┘ï ┘ê┘Ä╪ú┘Ä╪╡┘è┘Ç┘ä╪º .( ╪½┘Ä┘ä╪º╪½╪º┘ï )</ar>\n<ar>╪ú┘Ä╪╣┘Ç┘ê╪░┘Å ╪¿┘É╪º┘ä┘ä┘ç┘É ┘à┘É┘å┘Ä ╪º┘ä╪┤┘Ä┘æ┘Ç┘è┘Æ╪╖╪º┘å┘É</ar>\n<ar>┘à┘É┘å┘Æ ┘å┘Ä┘ü┘Æ╪«┘É┘Ç┘ç┘É ┘ê┘Ä┘å┘Ä┘ü┘Æ┘Ç╪½┘É┘ç┘É ┘ê┘Ä┘ç┘Ä┘à┘Æ┘Ç╪▓┘É┘ç </ar>\n\n<i><b>Transliteration:</b> Allahu 'Akbar Kabira, Allahu 'Akbar Kabira, Allahu 'Akbar Kabira, walhamdu lillahi kathira, walhamdu lillahi kathira, walhamdu lillahi kathira, wa Subhanallahi bukratan wa'asila. 'A `udhu billahi min ash-shaytan: min nafkhihi, wa nafthihi, wa hamzihi.</i>\n\n<b>Translation:</b> Allah is the Greatest, Most Great. Allah is the Greatest, Most Great. Allah is the Greatest, Most Great. Praise is to Allah, abundantly. Praise is to Allah, abundantly. Praise is to Allah, abundantly. Glory is to Allah, at the break of day and at its end. I seek refuge in Allah from Satan. From his breath, and from his voice, and from his whisper. [Abu Dawud 1/203, Ibn Majah 1/265, ai Ahmad 4/8<b>5.</b> Muslim recorded a similar Hadil 1/420]"
